Z||000000||Denny||05-27-2001||09:03 AM||||This appeared in the Lancaster (PA) Sunday News today, thought some of you might find it interesting:<P>"ON THIN ICE<BR>Police in Cumberland County have told organizers of car shows at the Carlisle Fairgrounds that authorities won't tolerate the ruckus caused by a recent show.<P>Responding the resident's complaints about noise, street racing and out-of-control parties at motels after the May 5-6 Custom Compact/Power Jam show, police chiefs of several departments met recently with John Kutsch, president of Carlisle Productions.<P>Police suggested that organizers tone down the show, which drew 25,000 people this year, by eliminating a bikini contest, band concert and smoking car tire demonstrations."<P>-Denny||||reg||1
